From 7ecf8b61dc44374d3cb1426903721232ae8ffe70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:49:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add TheTVDB absolute and alternate episode orders

SkyHook only publishes TheTVDB's aired order. With a TheTVDB v4 API key
(and PIN, for a user-supported key) saved, a series TheTVDB owns can now be
added with TheTVDB's absolute or alternate order, alongside the default
aired order, in the existing ordering dropdown.

- New Tvdb provider: v4 login with token caching and one retry on 401,
  paginated season-type fetch, 404 treated as "no such order".
- TvdbOrderingProjector renumbers SkyHook episodes by TheTVDB episode id.
  Unlisted episodes are kept; ones that would collide move to season 0.
- SkyHookProxy applies the ordering on add and refresh and rebuilds seasons.
  A vanished ordering throws rather than falling back to aired order.
- GET series/ordering takes tvdbId; settings gain TvdbApiKey and TvdbPin,
  masked like the TMDB key. Frontend settings and add dialog updated.

Verification: not compiled and tests not run (no .NET SDK or NuGet access in
the authoring environment). Frontend files parse and pass Prettier, but were
not typechecked. Not exercised against the live TheTVDB API.

